---
description: How agents run root commands on this machine
alwaysApply: true
---

Run root commands with plain `sudo`; the password prompt appears to the user as a popup (tmux popup or desktop dialog).

- Call `sudo` by name, without `-n` and not as `/usr/bin/sudo`; those skip the wrapper that shows the password prompt and fail with "a password is required".
- Never ask the user for their sudo password, and never try to read, pipe or echo it.
- If sudo fails with "cancelled or timed out", the user declined or was away; report it, don't retry in a loop.
